one("These notes no longer treat p28b_small as the 14.2 QC candidate, because its fit rests on row index pairs (PREREG37). The PREREG33 reassignment, which was never cleared, rests on the same pairs, and the QC anchor awaits a field tag refit. The same evidence bears on the shipped 0.111.",
    "These notes no longer treat p28b_small as the 14.2 QC candidate, because its fit rests on row index pairs (PREREG37). The PREREG33 reassignment, which was never cleared, rests on the same pairs. The same evidence bears on the shipped 0.111.\n\n"
    "PREREG38 refit a single anchor on fold A field tags (1.242). On fold B it brings the pooled predicted over observed height increment ratio to 1.053 (0.093 at 0.111), every diameter class within 0.04 m yr⁻¹ of zero and the dominant cohort to 0.994 of measured t2 height (0.898 at 0.111), but the published TOPHT bias is +16.21% against a limit of +14.63%, so it was not adopted. PREREG39 traced the conflict to the observed height rule: 60.6% of observed TOPHT heights come from the generic `himp` curve, which gives 0.892 of measured height, and that step carries 9.29 of the 16.78 point gap between TOPHT and the dominant cohort. PREREG40 rebuilt the top height gate on measured heights against a 10% ceiling taken from the FIA field measurement tolerance for tree length, a value still to be confirmed: the 1.242 arm is +1.60% (-0.05 to 3.25) and 0.111 is -8.45%, and PREREG41 confirmed the reading on the same trees on both sides (+1.50% and -8.82%). The ceiling is loose, since every arm tested passes it.\n\n"
    "The QC anchor track is closed with 0.111 kept for 14.2 (`2026-10-02_v142_qc-anchor_CLOSEOUT.md`). On measured tagged trees 0.111 predicts about a tenth of observed height increment, the dominant cohort reaches 0.90 of measured t2 height and measured top height is 8 to 9% low, so QC height and height driven outputs from 14.2 are biased low over long projections. PREREG42 also issued revision 3 of the PREREG19 result, which corrects the attribution of its tag match counts: 11,632 (1,569) are row index counts on the 378 qc_c stands that ran, and field tags give 10,226 (2,299).")
one("PREREG33 failed the same grid (Reineke 1.412 against 1.266). Both grids tested anchors fitted on row index pairs (PREREG37), so they bound what those anchors do and say nothing yet about a field tag anchor.",
    "PREREG33 failed the same grid (Reineke 1.412 against 1.266). Both grids tested anchors fitted on row index pairs (PREREG37). PREREG41 ran the same grid for the field tag anchor 1.242 against the frozen 14.1 trajectories and did not clear it either: three new basal area site ordering flags and a Reineke margin of 1.490 against 1.266, the same pattern as p28b_small. The margins are small and appear tied to the seedling start (stems rise from 1,000 to about 2,800 ha⁻¹ through ingrowth before any self thinning) and to the 2.5 m span of the QC ESI levels, but the rule was fixed before the grid was run and is not waived.")
